# Power

outfit "Quantum Vacuum Battery"
	category "Power"
	series "Batteries"
	index 91010
	cost 3000000
	thumbnail "outfit/quarg quantum battery"
	"mass" 50
	"outfit space" -50
	"energy capacity" 60000
	"active cooling" 25
	"cooling energy" 1.25
	description "Human engineers who first came into contact with the Quarg were astonished by the sheer energy density of their technology. This Quarg battery holds enough energy to level a small city, rumored to be stored in the negative quantum vacuum pressure between innumerable tiny plates. Somehow, the battery chills itself as energy is drained from it, seemingly in defiance of the human understanding of thermodynamics."


outfit "Antimatter Core"
	category "Power"
	series "Generators"
	index 91010
	cost 20000000
	thumbnail "outfit/quarg antimatter core"
	"mass" 50
	"outfit space" -50
	"energy generation" 12
	"heat generation" 10
	description "Although humanity is now capable of producing antimatter in relatively significant quantities when compared to a thousand years ago, it is still nothing next to the output of the Quarg, who can produce enough antimatter to outfit even civilian ships with an extremely compact Antimatter Core. This device releases extreme amounts of energy in a simple, elegant package, all while producing surprisingly little waste heat."


outfit "Singularity Core"
	category "Power"
	series "Generators"
	index 91020
	cost 50000000
	thumbnail "outfit/quarg singularity core"
	"mass" 400
	"outfit space" -80
	"energy generation" 23.5
	"heat generation" 22.5
	"inertia reduction" 0.15
	description "According to little more than vague allusions by the Quarg, these generators contain a minuscule black hole, spewing radiation as it is fed a trickle of mass. This black hole is small enough to output a truly staggering amount of energy via Hawking radiation, which grows in power as a black hole shrinks, something that suggests the black hole within the Singularity Core is truly microscopic."
	description "	Further wild guesses by scientists and conspiracy theorists alike allege that the Quarg are able to somehow trick the laws of physics themselves to make this black hole weigh far less than it otherwise should, bringing its mass from that of a small moon to something a ship could have a hope of moving."


outfit "Quasar Core"
	category "Power"
	series "Generators"
	index 91030
	cost 100000000
	thumbnail "outfit/quarg quasar core"
	"mass" 600
	"outfit space" -120
	"energy generation" 37.5
	"heat generation" 35
	"inertia reduction" 0.15
	description "This larger generator appears similar to the Singularity Core, only even more powerful. Little is known about its exact function, but purely based on its name, some have speculated that the Quasar Core's increased output is the result of the black hole at its core being fed enough mass to form a small accretion disk, releasing light and heat as it falls towards the event horizon and is compressed to an unimaginable degree."
	description "	While this process should be far less fuel-efficient than simply capturing the Hawking radiation emitted by the black hole alone, the staggering power density of this generator appears to be evidence it was worth the trade."


# Systems

outfit "Aspis Shield Generator"
	category "Systems"
	series "Shields"
	index 91010
	cost 5000000
	thumbnail "outfit/quarg aspis shield generator"
	"mass" 40
	"outfit space" -40
	"shield generation" 4
	"shield energy" 2
	"disruption protection" .2
	"piercing protection" .4
	description "Even the smallest example of Quarg shield generation displays defensive powers greater than what humans would normally consider to be sufficient."


outfit "Ancile Shield Generator"
	category "Systems"
	series "Shields"
	index 91020
	cost 7500000
	thumbnail "outfit/quarg ancile shield generator"
	"mass" 55
	"outfit space" -55
	"shield generation" 6.25
	"shield energy" 3.125
	"disruption protection" .3
	"piercing protection" .6
	description "In addition to being able to recover their shields more quickly and efficiently than any other technology of considerable size, Quarg shield generators also provide an impressive degree of protection against weapons designed to bypass shields entirely."


outfit "Aegis Shield Generator"
	category "Systems"
	series "Shields"
	index 91030
	cost 12500000
	thumbnail "outfit/quarg aegis shield generator"
	"mass" 80
	"outfit space" -80
	"shield generation" 10
	"shield energy" 5
	"disruption protection" .5
	"piercing protection" 1
	description "The first humans who met the Quarg thought that their technology worked on magic, and many even think so to this day. The mechanism by which this Quarg shield generator works is completely unknown to humanity, providing an astounding amount of protection, and the Quarg aren't interested in giving up the secrets behind it."


outfit "Peripheral Repair Hub"
	category "Systems"
	series "Repair"
	index 91010
	cost 2000000
	thumbnail "outfit/quarg peripheral repair hub"
	"mass" 25
	"outfit space" -25
	"fuel generation" 0.025
	"hull repair rate" 1
	"hull energy" .5
	description "The repair systems employed by the Quarg operate in ways that seem to defy reality, somehow gathering matter and injecting it into a ship's hull and fuel systems. This provides essential maintenance that benefits core aspects of spaceflight - durability, longevity, and most importantly, survivability."


outfit "Central Repair Hub"
	category "Systems"
	series "Repair"
	index 91020
	cost 5000000
	thumbnail "outfit/quarg central repair hub"
	"mass" 55
	"outfit space" -55
	"fuel generation" 0.07
	"hull repair rate" 2.5
	"hull energy" 1.25
	description "In a manner which is not easily discernible to humans, this system collects ambient matter in space and feeds it back to the ship from a large central hub of wires and tubes. The accumulated matter is then used to both regenerate the ship's hull and refill its fuel reserves."


